   "part": "The road to February",
   "text": "On the twenty-first of November 2013, a week before the European summit at Vilnius, Ukraine's government suspended preparations to sign the agreement. That night, protesters gathered on the Maidan. On the thirtieth of November, riot police violently cleared students from the square. The next day, a huge crowd filled central Kyiv. On the seventeenth of December, Russia announced it would buy up to fifteen billion dollars of Ukrainian government bonds, and sell gas more cheaply. It bought the first three billion that month. In January, parliament passed laws restricting protest. There were clashes on Hrushevskoho Street. On the twenty-second of January, two protesters were shot dead. A third man died of his wounds three days later. Another protester was abducted and found dead. The laws were repealed, and the prime minister resigned."
