   "part": "Crimea",
   "text": "In a documentary preview shown in March 2015, President Putin said that on the night of the twenty-second to the twenty-third of February 2014 he told officials to start work on what he called returning Crimea to Russia. Early on the twenty-seventh of February 2014, armed men without insignia seized the parliament of Crimea, in Simferopol. At first, President Putin said these were local self-defence forces. On the seventeenth of April, Putin said Russian troops had stood behind Crimea's self-defence forces. The European Court of Human Rights later found that Russia exercised effective control over Crimea from the twenty-seventh of February, for the purposes of the European human rights convention. What happened next is told on the following pages: Crimea, and then the war in the Donbas."
